Triage 6904291433 set the condition for this: "If the seat finds production boot (`os start` / serve) also double-evaluates, regrade p1." The dev measured real boots on main's composition, with a job handler reading state its `onEnable` bound. Production fails too: a non-host config under `os start` (createStandaloneStack plus the `hasAppPluginAlready` graft) left the state unset. Results by boot:
- host `os dev`: unset;
- host `os start`: bound;
- non-host `os dev`: unset;
- non-host `os start`: unset;
- artifact-only `os start`: unset. Its `onEnable` never runs, by the documented rule that an artifact carries no `onEnable`. That is not this defect.

The fix on `claude/area-A5-34179` changes the one graft that both serve sites call, so it covers the production path as well. The PR follows.
